WEBVTT

00:05:58.354 --> 00:06:01.065
that we don't change our minds
most of the time.

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:04.860
But we can better understand
opposing perspectives,

00:06:04.902 --> 00:06:08.614
which can help us to better advocate
for our own beliefs.

00:06:08.656 --> 00:06:11.117
And maybe, just maybe,

00:06:11.158 --> 00:06:13.744
it even allows us to reach a compromise

00:06:13.786 --> 00:06:15.704
when the situation demands it.

00:06:16.455 --> 00:06:18.999
So I think the question remains.

00:06:19.417 --> 00:06:23.504
How can we create space
for this kind of bipartisan discourse?

00:06:24.255 --> 00:06:28.384
Well, I think the first step
is finding a community.

00:06:28.759 --> 00:06:32.012
When I think back
to my experience in the ACLU,